  "id": "yellowstone",
  "intro": "Yellowstone is the region on this site where a radio is closest to genuinely necessary. There is effectively no cell coverage away from the villages, distances between services are enormous, and the Park Service runs an extensive analog VHF repeater network that will tell you about a road closure, a bison jam or a rescue long before you would find out any other way. Bring the federal band and a spare battery.",
  "introz": "黄石是本站所有地区中最接近“真的需要电台”的地方。离开村镇基本没有手机信号，服务点之间距离极远，而国家公园局运营着一套覆盖广泛的模拟 VHF 中继网络——封路、野牛堵车、救援，你会比通过任何其他途径都更早知道。记得带上联邦波段和备用电池。",
  "stations": [
    { "f": 172.475, "n": "Yellowstone NPS — main operations", "z": "黄石国家公园局主业务频率", "c": "parks", "m": "NFM", "conf": "check", "a": "Yellowstone National Park", "d": "Ranger dispatch for the whole park, relayed through repeaters on Mount Washburn and other high points so it covers a remarkable area. Road status, wildlife jams, medicals and law enforcement. Exact channels shift — scan 162–174 MHz in NFM on arrival and save what is busy.", "dz": "覆盖全园的护林员调度，通过 Washburn 山等高点中继转发，覆盖范围相当大。内容包括路况、野生动物堵车、医疗和执法。具体频率会变——到园后用 NFM 扫 162–174 MHz，把活跃的存下来。", "odds": 1 },
    { "f": 171.675, "n": "Yellowstone NPS — secondary", "z": "黄石公园局次要频率", "c": "parks", "m": "NFM", "conf": "check", "a": "Yellowstone National Park", "odds": 1 },
